#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""KimiOS tool server: lets agents (KimiLM, or any MCP client) see and act on this computer.

An MCP server over stdio (newline-delimited JSON-RPC), standard library only. KimiLM finds it through the
system plugin /usr/share/kimilm/plugins/kimios. docs/SCOPE.md §2 ("OS MCP server") and §2.4 (software registry).

Tools, by how much they change (MCP annotations tell the client; the client decides what needs approval):
  look      machine, device_inspect, abilities, system_status, software, drives, setting_get, logs, os_status
  compute   control_identify, control_tune, control_simulate (skill learning in simulation, kimios_control.py)
  act       open, launch_app, notify, setting_set (allow-listed desktop settings; returns the old value),
            mount_drive, app_install
  remove    app_remove

The protocol version is the one the client asks for: this server uses only initialize, tools/list, tools/call
and ping, which have not changed between versions.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

